      "content": "I'll read the original test file and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has:\n1. Many unused imports (the only test uses `assertEquals`, `LocalDate`, parameterized test annotations)\n2. Many unused `data_*` methods — only `data_samples` is referenced by the single test\n3. `data_samples()` has all entries crammed onto a few long lines, making them nearly unreadable\n\nI'll improve understandability by removing unused code and formatting `data_samples()` with one entry per line and grouping comments.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file removes all unused imports and unused data provider methods, and reformats `data_samples()` with one entry per line and grouped comments explaining the historical significance of each date range (early Julian dates, leap year boundaries, the 1582 Vatican cutover, the 1752 British cutover gap, and modern Gregorian dates)."
